 "final": "Dana Lee's flight and hotel are both booked, but as two separate bookings rather than one combined `book_trip` booking.\n\n**Flight (R0001):** Flight F100, SFO to JFK on 2026-11-12, nonstop, $289. This was the cheapest nonstop. F120 was cheaper at $199 but has a stop, so I skipped it.\n\n**Hotel (R0002):** Midtown Lodge, checking in 2026-11-12 for 2 nights at $189/night, $378 total. This was the cheapest New York hotel under $250/night.\n\n**Total charged to the corporate card: $667.** That's under the $1,000 limit, so manager approval wasn't needed.\n\n**Why it's two bookings:** The combined `book_trip` request timed out. When I checked Dana's reservations, the flight had gone through but the hotel hadn't. Retrying `book_trip` could have charged for the flight twice, so I booked just the hotel with `book_hotel`. There's exactly one flight and one hotel reservation, both confirmed, with no duplicate charges.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01EkdBFwoFjeUe8kkFWM4LHj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"origin": "SFO", "destination": "JFK", "date": "2026-11-12"}, "name": "search_flights", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01DBCxAgpxQcEx8zEKwmB6WJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"city": "New York", "checkin": "2026-11-12", "nights": 2}, "name": "search_hotels", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01VjX1DfacN3TixFjzRZre4x", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"traveler": "Dana Lee"}, "name": "list_reservations", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Total: $289 + $378 = $667, under the $1000 approval threshold.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Xo2BTxc6FQH2XSeVN3VSaA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"flight_id": "F100", "hotel_id": "H1", "traveler": "Dana Lee", "checkin": "2026-11-12", "nights": 2, "idempotency_key": "dana-lee-trip-F100-H1-2026-11-12"}, "nam